[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pallets/click/issues/comments/2147224623","html_url":"https://github.com/pallets/click/issues/2447#issuecomment-2147224623","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pallets/click/issues/2447","id":2147224623,"node_id":"IC_kwDOASN_zM5__Awv","user":{"login":"aplowman","id":5176471,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxNzY0NzE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5176471?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aplowman","html_url":"https://github.com/aplowman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aplowman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aplowman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aplowman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aplowman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aplowman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aplowman/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aplowman/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aplowman/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aplowman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-06-04T10:50:31Z","updated_at":"2024-06-04T10:50:31Z","body":"I came across this issue too and asked about it on StackOverflow [here](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/78572746/how-to-use-python-clicks-ctx-with-resource-to-capture-tracebacks-in-sub-com/78572866#78572866) (in my case, I'd like to print exception tracebacks to a file, and prevent them from printing to `stderr`). The solution offered was to override `Context.__exit__` so it forwards on the exception information:\r\n\r\n```py\r\nclass MyContext(click.Context):\r\n    def __exit__(self, exc_type, exc_value, tb):\r\n        self._depth -= 1\r\n        if self._depth == 0:\r\n            self._exit_stack.__exit__(exc_type, exc_value, tb)\r\n            self._exit_stack = contextlib.ExitStack()\r\n        click.core.pop_context()\r\n\r\ncli.context_class = MyContext\r\n```\r\n\r\nFor reference, the [current implementation](https://github.com/pallets/click/blob/923d197b56caa9ffea21edeef5baf1816585b099/src/click/core.py#L471) of `Context.__exit__` is essentially:\r\n\r\n```py\r\ndef __exit__(self, exc_type, exc_value, tb):\r\n    self._depth -= 1\r\n    if self._depth == 0:\r\n        self._exit_stack.close() # equivalent to: `self._exit_stack.__exit__(None, None, None)`\r\n        self._exit_stack = ExitStack()\r\n    pop_context()\r\n```\r\n\r\nSo it seems this would be a minor change to fix; although I have no idea if it would have undesirable side effects.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pallets/click/issues/comments/2147224623/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"aplowman","id":5176471,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxNzY0NzE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5176471?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aplowman","html_url":"https://github.com/aplowman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aplowman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aplowman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aplowman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aplowman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aplowman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aplowman/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aplowman/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aplowman/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aplowman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":15816812221,"node_id":"LE_lADOASN_zM5do5JozwAAAAOuwWa9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/palle